The '''2022 AFA World Cup''' was the 17th [[AFA World Cup]], the quadrennial international football tournament for men's senior national teams organised by the [[Adonian Football Association]] (AFA). The tournament was hosted by [[Shansi]] from 10 June to 10 July 2022. [[Balisca]] won the tournament for the fourth time, defeating [[Sanrobonia]] in the final at [[Heung Gong Stadium]], while [[Asikyira]] finished third and [[Burawa]] finished fourth.

The competition featured 36 teams divided into twelve groups of three. The top two teams from each group advanced to the knockout stage, with the eight best group winners receiving byes to the round of 16.

